{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"8bbbd3c101ef64eb","name":"card_event_exiled_forces","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/events/card_event_exiled_forces","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"EXILED FORCES","text":"Add a copy of target unit to your support line. Destroy it in 3 turns.","flavorText":"During WWII, thousands of Polish soldiers continued the fight from exile after Poland's defeat in 1939. These exiled forces regrouped in France, the United Kingdom, the Middle East, and later in Italy and Western Europe. Their resilience formed the backbone of the Polish Armed Forces in the West, a military force loyal to the Polish government-in-exile based in London. After the fall of France in 1940, many Polish troops evacuated to Britain. There, they rebuilt under British command, forming air, naval and ground units. Polish pilots played a key role in the Battle of Britain, especially in the famed No. 303 Squadron. On land, the 1st Armoured Division under General Stanisław Maczek distinguished itself in the Normandy campaign and the liberation of the Netherlands. In Italy, the 2nd Corps led by General Władysław Anders gained renown for its capture of Monte Cassino in 1944. Despite their sacrifices, many of these troops were barred from returning to postwar Poland, now under Soviet influence.","faction":"Poland","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_exiled_forces","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_exiled_forces_title","SourceString":"EXILED FORCES","LocalizedString":"EXILED FORCES"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_exiled_forces_text","SourceString":"Add a copy of target unit to your support line. Destroy it in 3 turns.","LocalizedString":"Add a copy of target unit to your support line. Destroy it in 3 turns."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_exiled_forces_history","SourceString":"During WWII, thousands of Polish soldiers continued the fight from exile after Poland's defeat in 1939. These exiled forces regrouped in France, the United Kingdom, the Middle East, and later in Italy and Western Europe. Their resilience formed the backbone of the Polish Armed Forces in the West, a military force loyal to the Polish government-in-exile based in London. After the fall of France in 1940, many Polish troops evacuated to Britain. There, they rebuilt under British command, forming air, naval and ground units. Polish pilots played a key role in the Battle of Britain, especially in the famed No. 303 Squadron. On land, the 1st Armoured Division under General Stanisław Maczek distinguished itself in the Normandy campaign and the liberation of the Netherlands. In Italy, the 2nd Corps led by General Władysław Anders gained renown for its capture of Monte Cassino in 1944. Despite their sacrifices, many of these troops were barred from returning to postwar Poland, now under Soviet influence.","LocalizedString":"During WWII, thousands of Polish soldiers continued the fight from exile after Poland's defeat in 1939. These exiled forces regrouped in France, the United Kingdom, the Middle East, and later in Italy and Western Europe. Their resilience formed the backbone of the Polish Armed Forces in the West, a military force loyal to the Polish government-in-exile based in London. After the fall of France in 1940, many Polish troops evacuated to Britain. There, they rebuilt under British command, forming air, naval and ground units. Polish pilots played a key role in the Battle of Britain, especially in the famed No. 303 Squadron. On land, the 1st Armoured Division under General Stanisław Maczek distinguished itself in the Normandy campaign and the liberation of the Netherlands. In Italy, the 2nd Corps led by General Władysław Anders gained renown for its capture of Monte Cassino in 1944. Despite their sacrifices, many of these troops were barred from returning to postwar Poland, now under Soviet influence."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Poland/10_Homefront/T_exiled_forces.T_exiled_forces","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/EXILED_FORCES.EXILED_FORCES","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":508.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_event_exiled_forces_photo","SourceString":"Hawker Hurricanes of RAF No. 303 Polish Squadron. Date unknown.","LocalizedString":"Hawker Hurricanes of RAF No. 303 Polish Squadron. Date unknown."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"Notes":"Image needed to be customized","isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"tmpCard","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_exiled_forces_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":true,"flags":"FUNC_Event | FUNC_Public | FUNC_HasOutParms | FUNC_BlueprintCallable | FUNC_BlueprintEvent","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarget","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_card","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_IsUnit_isIt","type":"bool","direction":"in"}],"body":[{"op